        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/165586925?u=6d43601892aeb133437bb3f53783109ff67e6834&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Description<br>\nAdds an introductory paragraph to the aria-busy attribute documentation. The new paragraph clearly explains the purpose of aria-busy as a global ARIA state that indicates when an element is being updated, helping assistive technologies understand when content is not ready to be read. It also highlights common use cases both inside and outside of ARIA live regions.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Motivation<br>\nThis addition improves clarity for developers by providing a straightforward explanation of aria-busy early in the document. It helps readers better understand how and why to use the attribute effectively, enhancing accessibility implementation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #32293.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2135571161\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32293\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/32293/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32293\">#32293</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/39854",
            "title": "docs(aria-busy): add intro paragraph explaining aria-busy purpose and use cases",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-08T01:16:04.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-08T01:14:02.000Z",
            "author": {
