        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n\n\n\n<hr>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As part of a larger project to make the challenges/reader exercises in MDN learn more consistent, this PR removes the inconsistently used \"Active learning...\" title from the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Structuring_content/Structuring_documents\" rel=\"nofollow\">Structuring documents</a> article.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There were no old code editors to remove in this article, but I also took the opportunity to improve the flow of the article, and get rid of the ugly hand-drawn diagrams.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/39831",
            "title": "Remove active learning, improve Structuring documents",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-06T15:17:32.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-06T15:15:10.000Z",
